"""B5819W - Schottky barrier diode, 40 V, 1 A, SOD-123.

Datasheet: Jiangsu Changjiang Electronics Technology (JCET) B5817W-B5819W, D, March 2015,
2 pages, LCSC C8598 ("DS"). LCSC lists the part as "B5819W SL", SL being its marking (DS p.1).

Maximum ratings (DS p.1, Ta = 25 C): VRM 40 V; VRRM, VRWM, VR 40 V; VR(RMS) 28 V; IO 1 A
average; IFSM 9 A (8.3 ms); IFRM 1.5 A; Pd 500 mW, derated linearly to 0 at 125 C (DS p.2
power derating curve); RthJA 200 C/W; TJ 125 C max; Tstg -55 to 150 C.
Electrical characteristics (DS p.1, Ta = 25 C): V(BR) 40 V min at 1 mA; IR 1 mA max at 40 V;
VF max 0.6 V at 1 A, 0.9 V at 3 A; CD 120 pF max at 4 V, 1 MHz.
Typical curves (DS p.2): VF about 0.3 V at 0.1 A and 0.5 V at 1 A (25 C); reverse current at
VR 17 V about 12 uA at 25 C, 0.12 mA at 75 C and 1.2 mA at 100 C; at VR 5 V about 6 uA,
70 uA and 0.6 mA.
Polarity (DS p.1 package view): the marking bar indicates the cathode.

Pins: pad 1 cathode (K), pad 2 anode (A): KiCad's D_SOD-123 footprint numbers the cathode pad 1
and marks it with its silkscreen bar. The datasheet gives no package drawing or land pattern; the
footprint is the KiCad library's SOD-123 land.

Application on the next main board (research/next-revision, power path; A.4): VBAT -> VSYS
OR-ing diode. The 4S pack (17.4 V with HV cells) sits at 44 % of VRRM. Forward: about 0.13 A at
14.8 V (L6981 and the analog LDO), about 46 mW with VF ~0.35 V, +9 K at 200 C/W. Reverse: the
diode only blocks while VSYS (USB VBUS, <= 5.25 V) is above a missing or switched-off pack, so VR
stays near 5 V; its leakage then back-feeds the switched VBAT node (inference).

This is the stdlib Rectifier generic's part, packaged because the generic cannot carry an MPN.
"""

A = io(Net)
K = io(Net)

Component(
    name="D",
    prefix="D",
    symbol=Symbol(library="B5819W.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("D_SOD-123.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="B5819W", manufacturer="JCET"),
    pins={
        "A": A,
        "K": K,
    },
)
